# Shipped with the artifact deliberately. Git on Windows checks out CRLF by
# default, and the public CI run on 24 Oct 2026 failed both Windows legs because
# of it: the docs-honesty regexes match ```bash\n, a CRLF checkout makes that
# ```bash\r\n, zero command blocks were found, and the test then failed on the
# emptiness check. The engine itself is CRLF-safe (verified), so this is about
# the repo being consistent for anyone who clones it on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf
